// The relief of having put it into something that could take it. Written on
// the aggressor's side of a brawl, and it is load-bearing rather than
// flavour: `Disgruntled` ratchets and never eases, so without something
// pushing back a program past `MORALE_LASHES_OUT_AT` would fight every time
// the roll came up for the rest of the run.
//
// Short-lived and capped low on purpose. One vent does not clear that hole
// and is not meant to — a badly-run base does descend into repeated fighting
// — but the meter moves the right way, and it must never be worth *farming*
// morale by starting fights.
(
    id: "vented",
    name: "Let it out",
    blurb: "Put it into something that could take it.",
    valence: 5.0,
    half_life: 2000,
    subject: Nothing,
    strike_cap: 3,
)
